      "    label: 'L2 正确性与健壮性',\n",
      "    prompt: base + `\n",
      "\n",
      "YOUR SCOPE — cross-cutting correctness & robustness review of the WHOLE project:\n",
      "Read /home/pika/work/bingoagent/src/mc_bingo_agent/app.py fully plus the Java hook files.\n",
      "Hunt for: race conditions, unhandled exceptions (especially in threads and Qt slots), malformed-input handling (API JSON, SSE fragments split across chunks, tool-call JSON, JVM state JSON, CLI args, socket payloads), network failure paths (timeouts, connection reset, partial reads), retry behavior, resource leaks (timers, sockets, threads, subprocesses, file handles), history file corruption, state-file staleness, daemon crash vs degrade behavior, and the interplay between the uncommitted WIP (inline chat input, IME env) and existing code. Concrete evidence required for each finding.`\n",
      "  },\n",
      "  {\n",
      "    label: 'L2 安全',\n",
      "    prompt: base + `\n",
      "\n",
      "YOUR SCOPE — cross-cutting SECURITY review of the WHOLE project:\n",
      "Read /home/pika/work/bingoagent/src/mc_bingo_agent/app.py fully, the Java hook files, systemd/mc-bingo-agent.service, .env.example.\n",
      "Analyze: API key handling (env file loading, exposure via process env / /proc / logs / errors), unix socket security (path, permissions, symlink attacks, who can connect, payload validation — can an unprivileged local user trigger arbitrary prompts or inject?), subprocess usage (shell injection in javac/jar/jps/attach commands), path traversal or arbitrary file read/write via config env vars or JVM state file, Java attach security (attaching to arbitrary JVM, loading agent jar from writable cache dir), secrets in error messages, model output rendered into the Qt overlay (rich text / HTML injection), history file permissions, and the WIP fcitx env changes. Mark each with concrete evidence and a fix.`\n",
      "  },\n",
      "  {\n",
      "    label: 'L2 重复与可维护性',\n",
      "    prompt: base + `\n",
      "\n",
      "YOUR SCOPE — cross-cutting duplication & maintainability review of the WHOLE project:\n",
      "Read /home/pika/work/bingoagent/src/mc_bingo_agent/app.py fully, all files under java_hook/src/mc/bingo/hook/, pyproject.toml, systemd/mc-bingo-agent.service, .env.example.\n",
      "Analyze: the V1/V2/V3/V4 Java duplication (three files of exactly 674 lines — quantify the actual diff between V3 and V4 and V2), repeated patterns inside app.py (e.g. repeated JSON/error handling, repeated socket send logic, repeated path env handling), magic numbers (6000 char cap, timers, retry counts), config sprawl (many MC_BINGO_* env vars + systemd Environment duplication with _ensure_qt_ime_env), dead code and unused imports, missing tooling (no tests, no ruff/lint config, no CI, no type checking), README/env drift. Recommend concrete, minimal-effort consolidation with file/line evidence.`\n",
      "  }\n",
      "];\n",
      "\n",
      "const verifyPrompt = (findings) => `You are the ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION layer of a clustered code review for /home/pika/work/bingoagent (Minecraft Bingo agent: PyQt5 daemon app.py + Java JVM hook java_hook/ + systemd + packaging).\n",
      "\n",
      "Below is the merged finding list produced by earlier review layers (JSON array). Every entry has: id, severity, category, file, location, title, description, evidence, suggested_fix.\n",
